as","/farmland-atlas/kansas/sumner-county"],["ARC or PLC in Sumner County","/arc-plc/kansas/sumner-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record for Sumner County runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 12 grids January to February came in under 90% of normal in 40 of those years. In 2025, the middle of the grids got 24% of normal in February to March and 207% in June to July. In 2026, May to June came in at 165% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 20229 had its driest year in 1956, at 45% of normal.</p>"}
